    "tranche": "T4",
    "tranche_reason": "The study uses sharpness minimization as a training method for robust generalization against photon-limited corruptions. Its results concern corrupted distributions, not the in-distribution claims or specific measures in the listed versions.",
    "gate_note": "The study evaluates corrupted test distributions, which the claim explicitly separates from its in-distribution versions. Table 3 directly ablates sharpness minimization and worst-case data selection; the remaining method comparisons do not test a listed version.",
    "test_reason": "SharpDRO uses sharpness minimization to improve corrupted-image classification and reports its method's performance. It does not test V7's magnitude-aware sharpness–generalization-gap correlation: Eq. 6 uses an absolute perturbation bound, and the experiments do not rank training–test gaps against sharpness or competing measures. No experiment tests V1–V6 or V8. Corrupted data alone do not establish exclusion; the measured constructs and comparisons do.",
    "authors_conclusion": "The record's paraphrase is accurate: the authors conclude that minimizing sharpness on worst-case data improves robustness to severe simulated corruptions, in both distribution-aware and distribution-agnostic settings, relative to the reported baselines. Their overall conclusion does not establish superiority in every table cell.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "SharpDRO combines worst-case data selection with sharpness minimization; experiments use Wide ResNet-28-2, SGD, and photon-limited corruption settings.",
    "method_sensitivity": "Corruption type and severity; perturbation scale ρ; distribution-aware versus distribution-agnostic data selection.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "Table 3 reports SharpDRO accuracy above both SAM and GroupDRO at Gaussian-noise severities 1–5 on CIFAR10. At severity 5, accuracies are 84.7%, 75.4%, and 78.2%, respectively. On clean data, SAM reaches 93.2% versus SharpDRO's 92.9%. These are training-method comparisons, not measurements of V7's correlation.",
        "proposed_claim": "Combining worst-case data selection with sharpness minimization can improve corrupted-image test accuracy relative to SAM and GroupDRO, with a small clean-accuracy tradeoff relative to SAM in this setting.",
